	"identifying_description": null,
	"web_text": "Trees do not grow in the tundra around the Bering Sea, but driftwood is carried to the area by the swollen springtime waters of the Kuskokwim and Yukon Rivers. Like all natural materials, driftwood was appreciated and treated with respect and reverence in the Far North. This storage container was carved in the shape of a seal from a single piece of wood, the grain of which was enhanced by a rich ocher stain. The container’s hinged lid is held closed by a delicate bird-bone pin. Fine Arts Museums of San Francisco, Yua, Spirit of the Arctic: Highlights from the Thomas G. Fowler Collection (New York: DelMonico Books | Prestel, 2020), p. 86, entry by Hillary C. Olcott.",
